scale. It was demolished in 2003.","subtitle":"Kentish Town","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/interaction-centre.jpg","external":"http://www.audacity.org/SM-26-11-07-02.htm","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/Kentish+Town/@51.55031,-0.14071,14z","also":[{"slug":"hans-ulrich-obrist","name":"Hans Ulrich Obrist","time":500.68,"topicId":"thinking","topicLabel":"Thinking"},{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":411.76,"topicId":"building","topicLabel":"Building"},{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":580.12,"topicId":"interaction-centre","topicLabel":"INTERACTION CENTRE"},{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":1022.52,"topicId":"enabling","topicLabel":"Enabling"},{"slug":"paul-finch","name":"Paul Finch","time":632.24,"topicId":"building","topicLabel":"Building"},{"slug":"peter-murray","name":"Peter Murray","time":1300.44,"topicId":"enabling","topicLabel":"Enabling"},{"slug":"will-alsop","name":"Will Alsop","time":15.88,"topicId":"interaction-centre","topicLabel":"INTERACTION CENTRE"}]},"Listed Building":{"slug":"listed-building","body":"A listed building, in the United Kingdom, is a building that has been placed on the Statutory List of Buildings of Special Architectural or Historic Interest. It is a widely used status, applied to around half a million buildings. The statutory body maintaining the list in <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/England\">England</a> is <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_Heritage\">English Heritage</a>.","subtitle":"English Heritage","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/listed-building.png","external":"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Listed_building","location":"https://maps.google.com/?q=UK","also":[{"slug":"brett-steele","name":"Brett Steele","time":328.96,"topicId":"influence","topicLabel":"Influence"},{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":593.8,"topicId":"interaction-centre","topicLabel":"INTERACTION CENTRE"},{"slug":"paul-finch","name":"Paul Finch","time":715.24,"topicId":"time","topicLabel":"Time"}]},"Paul Finch":{"slug":"paul-finch","body":"<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Paul is programme director of the World Architecture Festival and editorial director of the Architectural Review and Architects’ Journal. He has more than 40 years’ experience as a journalist, working for Estates Times (deputy editor, 1976-83), Building Design (editor, 1983-94) Architects’ Journal (editor, 1994-99), Architectural Review (editor, 2005-09), and Planning in London (joint editor since 1994).</p>","subtitle":"Architectural critic","image":"/cedric-price-memory-bank/cards/paul-finch.jpg","external":"http://www.designcouncil.org.uk/about-us/our-experts/paul-finch-obe","location":"https://www.google.com/maps/place/London,+UK/@51.5073509,-0.1277583,7z","also":[{"slug":"jeremy-melvin","name":"Jeremy Melvin","time":625.8,"topicId":"interaction-centre","topicLabel":"INTERACTION CENTRE"},{"slug":"max-neal","name":"Max Neal","time":410.92,"topicId":"office","topicLabel":"Office"}]}}}